<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ba Maw</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ba Maw was a Burmese lawyer and politician who served as the first premier of British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> from 1937 to 1939. During the Japanese occupation he became head of the Japanese-sponsored State of Burma, declared independent in 1943. After the war he was briefly imprisoned and never regained real political influence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ba-maw.jpg" alt="Ba Maw" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ba_Maw_portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
